{"id":"mahabharata-7-040","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":40,"title":"चत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 40 · Abhimanyu cuts down the Kaurava army","summary":{"en":"Abhimanyu roars and draws his bow again and again, covering the sky with arrows that blot out sight. He moves through the Kaurava army like Indra's grandson, in the midst of armour, heads and fallen limbs.","kn":"ಅಭಿಮನ್ಯು ಗರ್ಜಿಸಿ ಮತ್ತೆ ಮತ್ತೆ ಬಿಲ್ಲು ಎಳೆದು ಆಕಾಶವನ್ನು ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಮುಚ್ಚುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇಂದ್ರನ ಮೊಮ್ಮಗನಂತೆ ಕವಚ, ತಲೆ, ಅಂಗಗಳು ಬಿದ್ದ ಕೌರವ ಸೈನ್ಯದ ನಡುವೆ ಸಂಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अभिमन्यु गरजकर बार-बार धनुष खींचता है और बाणों से आकाश ढक देता है। वह इन्द्र के पौत्र की तरह कवच, सिरों और कटे अंगों से भरी कौरव सेना में विचरता है।","te":"అభిమన్యుడు గర్జించి మళ్లీ మళ్లీ విల్లు ఎక్కుపెట్టి బాణాలతో ఆకాశాన్ని కప్పుతాడు. ఇంద్రుని మనుమనిలా కవచాలు, తలలు, తెగిన అవయవాలతో నిండిన కౌరవసేనలో సంచరిస్తాడు.","ta":"அபிமன்யு முழங்கி மீண்டும் மீண்டும் வில்லை வளைத்து அம்புகளால் வானை மூடுகிறான். இந்திரனின் பேரன் போல் கவசம், தலைகள், வெட்டுண்ட உறுப்புகள் நிறைந்த கௌரவப் படையில் சுழல்கிறான்.","ml":"അഭിമന്യു ഗർജിച്ച് വില്ലെടുത്ത് ആവർത്തിച്ച് അമ്പുകൾ തൊടുക്കുന്നു; കാഴ്ച മറയ്ക്കുന്ന അമ്പുകൾകൊണ്ട് ആകാശം മൂടുന്നു. കവചങ്ങളുടെയും തലകളുടെയും വീണ അവയവങ്ങളുടെയും ഇടയിലൂടെ ഇന്ദ്രന്റെ പേരക്കുട്ടിയെപ്പോലെ അദ്ദേഹം കൗരവ സേനയിലൂടെ നീങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.40; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"अभिमन्युवधपर्व","titleEn":"Abhimanyuvadha Parva (Slaying of Abhimanyu)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सोऽभिगर्जन्धनुष्पाणिर्ज्यां विकर्षन्पुनः पुनः ।\nतयोर्महात्मनोस्तूर्णं रथान्तरमवापतत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Roaring, bow in hand, drawing the string again and again, he quickly came in between the two great-souled men's chariots."}},{"n":2,"text":"सोऽविध्यद्दशभिर्बाणैरभिमन्युं दुरासदम् ।\nसच्छत्रध्वजयन्तारं साश्वमाशु स्मयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced the unassailable Abhimanyu with ten arrows, along with his umbrella, banner, charioteer and horses, quickly, as if smiling."}},{"n":3,"text":"पितृपैतामहं कर्म कुर्वाणमतिमानुषम् ।\nदृष्ट्वार्दितं शरैः कार्ष्णिं त्वदीया हृषिताभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Krishna's son, who did superhuman deeds like those of his father and grandfather, tormented by arrows, your men were delighted."}},{"n":4,"text":"तस्याभिमन्युरायम्य स्मयन्नेकेन पत्रिणा ।\nशिरः प्रच्यावयामास स रथात्प्रापतद्भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abhimanyu, smiling, drew his bow and with a single arrow knocked off his head, and he fell from his chariot to the ground."}},{"n":5,"text":"कर्णिकारमिवोद्धूतं वातेन मथितं नगात् ।\nभ्रातरं निहतं दृष्ट्वा राजन्कर्णो व्यथां ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a karnikara tree torn up and broken by the wind from a mountain, he fell; seeing his brother killed, Karna, O king, was pained."}},{"n":6,"text":"विमुखीकृत्य कर्णं तु सौभद्रः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ।\nअन्यानपि महेष्वासांस्तूर्णमेवाभिदुद्रुवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having turned Karna away with heron-feathered arrows, Subhadra's son quickly attacked other great archers too."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततस्तद्विततं जालं हस्त्यश्वरथपत्तिमत् ।\nझषः क्रुद्ध इवाभिन्ददभिमन्युर्महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that spread-out net of elephants, horses, chariots and foot soldiers, the greatly renowned Abhimanyu tore like an angry fish."}},{"n":8,"text":"कर्णस्तु बहुभिर्बाणैरर्द्यमानोऽभिमन्युना ।\nअपायाज्जवनैरश्वैस्ततोऽनीकमभिद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tormented by many arrows from Abhimanyu, Karna fled on swift horses, and then the division was broken."}},{"n":9,"text":"शलभैरिव चाकाशे धाराभिरिव चावृते ।\nअभिमन्योः शरै राजन्न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Abhimanyu's arrows, like locusts in the sky or streams of rain, nothing could be made out, O king."}},{"n":10,"text":"तावकानां तु योधानां वध्यतां निशितैः शरैः ।\nअन्यत्र सैन्धवाद्राजन्न स्म कश्चिदतिष्ठत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of your warriors, being killed by sharp arrows, no one stood firm, O king, except the Sindhu king."}},{"n":11,"text":"सौभद्रस्तु ततः शङ्खं प्रध्माप्य पुरुषर्षभः ।\nशीघ्रमभ्यपतत्सेनां भारतीं भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Subhadra's son, best of men, blew his conch and quickly fell on the Bharata army, O best of Bharatas."}},{"n":12,"text":"स कक्षेऽग्निरिवोत्सृष्टो निर्दहंस्तरसा रिपून् ।\nमध्ये भारतसैन्यानामार्जुनिः पर्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a fire let loose in dry grass, burning his enemies with force, Arjuna's son ranged in the middle of the Bharata armies."}},{"n":13,"text":"रथनागाश्वमनुजानर्दयन्निशितैः शरैः ।\nस प्रविश्याकरोद्भूमिं कबन्धगणसंकुलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tormenting chariots, elephants, horses and men with sharp arrows, he entered and made the earth crowded with headless trunks."}},{"n":14,"text":"सौभद्रचापप्रभवैर्निकृत्ताः परमेषुभिः ।\nस्वानेवाभिमुखान्घ्नन्तः प्राद्रवञ्जीवितार्थिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cut down by the fine arrows sped from Subhadra's son's bow, they fled, desiring life, striking at their own facing them."}},{"n":15,"text":"ते घोरा रौद्रकर्माणो विपाठाः पृथवः शिताः ।\nनिघ्नन्तो रथनागाश्वाञ्जग्मुराशु वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those fierce, terrible, wide, sharp vipathas, killing chariots, elephants and horses, quickly went into the earth."}},{"n":16,"text":"सायुधाः साङ्गुलित्राणाः सखड्गाः साङ्गदा रणे ।\nदृश्यन्ते बाहवश्छिन्ना हेमाभरणभूषिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arms severed, with weapons, finger-guards, swords and armlets, adorned with golden ornaments, were seen in the battle."}},{"n":17,"text":"शराश्चापानि खड्गाश्च शरीराणि शिरांसि च ।\nसकुण्डलानि स्रग्वीणि भूमावासन्सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arrows, bows, swords, bodies and heads with earrings and garlands lay by thousands on the ground."}},{"n":18,"text":"अपस्करैरधिष्ठानैरीषादण्डकबन्धुरैः ।\nअक्षैर्विमथितैश्चक्रैर्भग्नैश्च बहुधा रथैः ।\nशक्तिचापायुधैश्चापि पतितैश्च महाध्वजैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With broken chariots in many ways, with fittings, platforms, pole and railings, axles and wheels shattered, with spears, bows and weapons, and great banners fallen,"}},{"n":19,"text":"निहतैः क्षत्रियैरश्वैर्वारणैश्च विशां पते ।\nअगम्यकल्पा पृथिवी क्षणेनासीत्सुदारुणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"and with slain Kshatriyas, horses and elephants, O lord of men, the earth in a moment became terrible and almost impassable."}},{"n":20,"text":"वध्यतां राजपुत्राणां क्रन्दतामितरेतरम् ।\nप्रादुरासीन्महाशब्दो भीरूणां भयवर्धनः ।\nस शब्दो भरतश्रेष्ठ दिशः सर्वा व्यनादयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the princes were killed and cried to one another, a great noise rose, increasing the fear of the cowards; that noise, O best of the Bharatas, made all directions resound."}},{"n":21,"text":"सौभद्रश्चाद्रवत्सेनां निघ्नन्नश्वरथद्विपान् ।\nव्यचरत्स दिशः सर्वाः प्रदिशश्चाहितान्रुजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Subhadra's son rushed at the army, killing horses, chariots and elephants, ranging in all directions and intermediate directions, breaking his enemies."}},{"n":22,"text":"तं तदा नानुपश्याम सैन्येन रजसावृतम् ।\nआददानं गजाश्वानां नृणां चायूंषि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"We could not see him then, hidden in dust raised by the army, as he took the lives of elephants, horses and men, O Bharata."}},{"n":23,"text":"क्षणेन भूयोऽपश्याम सूर्यं मध्यंदिने यथा ।\nअभिमन्युं महाराज प्रतपन्तं द्विषद्गणान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a moment we saw Abhimanyu again, tormenting hosts of foes like the sun at midday, O great king."}},{"n":24,"text":"स वासवसमः संख्ये वासवस्यात्मजात्मजः ।\nअभिमन्युर्महाराज सैन्यमध्ये व्यरोचत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like Indra in battle, grandson of Indra's son, Abhimanyu shone in the middle of the army, O great king."}}]}]}